ENTRY 9559 {"id":9559,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"packages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/README.md:316:  onStdout: (chunk) => process.stdout.write(chunk),\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/README.md:319:await cat.closeStdin();\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/README.md:328:- **Consuming output**: pass `onStdout`/`onStderr`, iterate `handle.events`, or call `handle.wait()` (which discards the output). These are mutually exclusive — `events` throws once callbacks or `wait()` are in use — except that `wait()` takes over from an `events` loop you have left. Nothing is buffered on the SDK side: until one of them is in use the stream is not read, and the process blocks once its pipe fills. Output arrives as `Uint8Array`, since a multi-byte character can straddle two chunks. If a callback throws, the process is killed and `wait()` rejects with that error.\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/README.md:330:- **Control calls**: `write(data)` (strings are UTF-8; large payloads are sent in sequential chunks), `closeStdin()` (EOF), `signal(\"SIGINT\" | \"SIGTERM\" | \"SIGKILL\")` and `kill()` (delivered to the whole process group), and `resize({ cols, rows })`. Each takes its own `timeoutMs`/`signal`. After the process has exited they fail with a `SandboxdRpcError`: `not_found` once sandboxd has forgotten the process, but a call made shortly after the exit (even after `wait()` has resolved) can first fail with another code, such as `internal`; `resize()` on a process without a PTY fails with `failed_precondition`. For a PTY process `closeStdin()` is rejected: it would close the terminal itself, so send `\"\\x04\"` (Ctrl-D) with `write()` instead.\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/sandbox.ts:606:  async closeLocal(): Promise<void> {\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/sandbox.ts:1169:    for (const name of [\"onStdout\", \"onStderr\"] as const) {\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/sandbox.ts:1246:          onStdout: opts?.onStdout,\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/types.ts:224:  onStdout?(chunk: Uint8Array): void;\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/commands.ts:127: * either by passing `onStdout`/`onStderr` to `start()`, by iterating\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/commands.ts:161:    private readonly callbacks: Pick<StartOptions, \"onStdout\" | \"onStderr\">,\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/commands.ts:173:    if (callbacks.onStdout || callbacks.onStderr) {\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/commands.ts:283:  async closeStdin(opts?: ProcessCallOptions): Promise<void> {\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/commands.ts:287:        'closeStdin() is not supported for a PTY process; write(\"\\\\x04\") instead',\npackages/vendor/agent-sandbox-client/src/commands.ts:395:        if (event.type === \"stdout\") this.callbacks.onStdout?.(event.data);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/local-bridge.ts:1:// Test-only bridge executable: the real runBridge, but \"the sandbox\" is a local pi-env daemon.\npackages/sandbox-env/test/local-bridge.ts:4:import { runBridge } from \"../src/bridge.ts\";\npackages/sandbox-env/test/local-bridge.ts:7:const code = await runBridge({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:4:import { runBridge } from \"../src/bridge.ts\";\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:23:describe(\"runBridge\", () => {\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:29:    const code = await runBridge({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:49:    const code = await runBridge({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:66:    const code = await runBridge({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:94:    const code = await runBridge({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:116:    const code = await runBridge({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:128:    const code = await runBridge({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:140:    const code = await runBridge({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:154:    const code = await runBridge({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:3:import { StartGate, gatedStart } from \"../src/start-gate.ts\";\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:7:describe(\"StartGate\", () => {\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:9:    const gate = new StartGate(5_000);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:29:    const gate = new StartGate(30);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:37:    const gate = new StartGate(5_000);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:53:describe(\"gatedStart\", () => {\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:55:    const gate = new StartGate(5_000);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:56:    const a = gatedStart(gate, [\"bridge\", \"--claim\", \"a\"]);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:57:    const b = gatedStart(gate, [\"bridge\", \"--claim\", \"b\"]);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:72:    const gate = new StartGate(5_000);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:73:    const a = gatedStart(gate, [\"a\"]);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:74:    const b = gatedStart(gate, [\"b\"]);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:84:    const gate = new StartGate(5_000);\npackages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:85:    const a = gatedStart(gate, [\"a\"]);\npackages/sandbox-env/src/start-gate.ts:9:export class StartGate {\npackages/sandbox-env/src/start-gate.ts:46:export function gatedStart(gate: StartGate, argv: readonly string[]): GatedStart {\npackages/sandbox-env/src/bridge.ts:59:export async function runBridge(options: BridgeOptions): Promise<number> {\npackages/sandbox-env/src/bridge.ts:71:  // Tells the parent that the cold start (the CPU-heavy part) is over; see StartGate.\npackages/sandbox-env/src/index.ts:4:import { StartGate, gatedStart } from \"./start-gate.js\";\npackages/sandbox-env/src/index.ts:7:const startGate = new StartGate(45_000);\npackages/sandbox-env/src/index.ts:9:export { runBridge } from \"./bridge.js\";\npackages/sandbox-env/src/index.ts:51:  const start = gatedStart(startGate, [\npackages/sandbox-env/src/cli.ts:2:import { runBridge } from \"./bridge.js\";\npackages/sandbox-env/src/cli.ts:14:  return runBridge({\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:5:  connectSandboxEnv,\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:30:const BRIDGE_LAUNCHER = fileURLToPath(new URL(\"./bridge-launcher.js\", import.meta.url));\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:328:    // pi-env protocol to the daemon, never through the bridge process environment (bridge-launcher derives its own claim's token and drops the master).\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:330:    return connectSandboxEnv({\npackages/orchestrator/src/bridge-launcher.ts:28:    throw new Error(\"bridge-launcher: --claim <name> is required\");\npackages/orchestrator/src/bridge-launcher.ts:44:    throw new Error(`bridge-launcher: ${ENV.masterKey} is not set`);\n","isError":false}]}
